From a9d2e9714ab11801255f01d3afecb958b409fe66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nipuna H Herath <nipunaherath@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:04:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] CUDA/HIP: the layer residual of Inkling 2 inside the
 one-token conv step

The attention-out and FFN-out short convolutions are followed by the layer
residual, l = inp + conv_out, as a separate ADD kernel. When that ADD comes
right after a fused conv step and nothing else reads the step's output, the
step's kernel now writes inp + y instead of y (the ADD's own float add, so
bit-identical). The graph expands l_out at the end of each layer, so the
next layer's conv-state gather no longer lands between the FFN-out step and
its residual.

R9700 Inkling-2-Mini UD-Q8_K_XL: 1,500 -> 1,412 kernels per generated token;
tg128 59.0 -> 59.9 tok/s (+1.6%). KLD against the previous commit,
wiki.test.raw -c 512, -ub 512 and -ub 1: 0. test-backend-ops SSM_CONV_STEP
gains residual cases (n_conv 2-4, a channel offset).
